{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011ChBzU4wNtFv9ADh6Bn5WG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can't see the project files or the database. Bash is disabled and no file-reading tool is loaded, so I can't identify the table. Instead, this block finds the unindexed foreign key at runtime. It aborts without changes unless exactly one is found.\n\n```sql\nDO $$\nDECLARE\n  cnt   int;\n  tbl   regclass;\n  col   name;\n  cname name;\nBEGIN\n  -- Foreign keys whose referencing table has no index leading with the FK column\n  WITH missing AS (\n    SELECT c.conname, c.conrelid, c.conkey[1] AS attnum\n    FROM pg_constraint c\n    JOIN pg_class t     ON t.oid = c.conrelid\n    JOIN pg_namespace n ON n.oid = t.relnamespace\n    WHERE c.contype = 'f'\n      AND n.nspname NOT IN ('pg_catalog', 'information_schema')\n      AND NOT EXISTS (\n        SELECT 1 FROM pg_index i\n        WHERE i.indrelid = c.conrelid\n          AND i.indkey[0] = c.conkey[1]\n      )\n  )\n  SELECT count(*) INTO cnt FROM missing;\n\n  IF cnt <> 1 THEN\n    RAISE EXCEPTION 'expected exactly 1 unindexed foreign key, found %; no changes made', cnt;\n  END IF;\n\n  WITH missing AS (\n    SELECT c.conname, c.conrelid, c.conkey[1] AS attnum\n    FROM pg_constraint c\n    JOIN pg_class t     ON t.oid = c.conrelid\n    JOIN pg_namespace n ON n.oid = t.relnamespace\n    WHERE c.contype = 'f'\n      AND n.nspname NOT IN ('pg_catalog', 'information_schema')\n      AND NOT EXISTS (\n        SELECT 1 FROM pg_index i\n        WHERE i.indrelid = c.conrelid\n          AND i.indkey[0] = c.conkey[1]\n      )\n  )\n  SELECT m.conrelid::regclass, a.attname, m.conname\n    INTO tbl, col, cname\n  FROM missing m\n  JOIN pg_attribute a ON a.attrelid = m.conrelid AND a.attnum = m.attnum;\n\n  EXECUTE format('CREATE INDEX %I ON %s (%I)', left('idx_' || cname, 63), tbl, col);\nEND $$;\n```\n\nThis uses a plain `CREATE INDEX`, not `CONCURRENTLY`, because a `DO` block runs inside a transaction. That takes a write lock on the table while the index builds."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":246,"cache_read_input_tokens":13321,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":246},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d03f6f3-343a-441e-9787-d83559c8833b","uuid":"230b75fe-6493-49ca-9da9-55e76056095b","timestamp":"2026-11-19T08:44:10.969Z","request_id":"req_011ChBzU4bJ19V7yjPGquVT9"}
